               ],
               "criterion": "Gives -1 as the limit of cos(pi g(x)); cos(-pi) left unevaluated is accepted.",
               "eligible_only_if": [],
               "check": null
            }
         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "c",
         "prompt": "Find \\( \\displaystyle \\lim_{x \\to 2} \\frac{f(x)\\,h(x)}{x^{2} - 4} \\) and \\( \\displaystyle \\lim_{x \\to 2} \\frac{x^{2} - 4}{h(x)} \\). Show the work that leads to your answers.",
         "setup_required": false,
         "answer_latex": "3, \\quad 1",
         "worked_solution": [
            {
               "text": "The denominator tends to 0, so the quotient theorem cannot be applied directly. Factor x^2 - 4.",
               "latex": "\\frac{f(x)\\,h(x)}{x^{2} - 4} = \\frac{h(x)}{x - 2} \\cdot \\frac{f(x)}{x + 2}"
            },
            {
               "text": "Each factor has a limit.",
               "latex": "\\lim_{x \\to 2} \\frac{f(x)\\,h(x)}{x^{2} - 4} = 4 \\cdot \\frac{3}{4} = 3"
            },
            {
               "text": "Invert the given quotient, whose limit 4 is not 0.",
               "latex": "\\frac{x^{2} - 4}{h(x)} = (x + 2) \\cdot \\frac{x - 2}{h(x)}"
            },
            {
               "text": "Evaluate.",
               "latex": "\\lim_{x \\to 2} \\frac{x^{2} - 4}{h(x)} = 4 \\cdot \\frac{1}{4} = 1"
            }
         ],
         "points": [
            {
               "point_id": "c1",
               "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99004",
               "skills": [
                  "BC-SKL-01019",
                  "BC-SKL-01020"
               ],
               "criterion": "Gives 3 as the limit of f(x)h(x)/(x^2 - 4). A response that applies the quotient theorem with denominator limit 0, or reports the limit as undefined or 0/0, does not earn the point.",
               "eligible_only_if": [],
